  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les capacit&#xe9;s institutionnelles des organisations de travailleurs sont renforc&#xe9;es</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The ILO&apos;s Country Programme Outcome (CPO) aims to enhance the institutional capacities of trade unions in Burundi, a country grappling with economic instability and weakened labor representation. With a focus on organizing vulnerable groups, particularly workers in the informal economy, the initiative seeks to empower these individuals and promote their integration into viable trade unions. This is critical in a context where deep poverty and the impacts of the COVID-19 pandemic have disproportionately affected informal workers, limiting their access to decent work opportunities and labor rights.

Through collaboration with local labor organizations, the CPO will advocate for the incorporation of decent work principles into national policies related to conflict prevention and economic recovery. The expected outcomes include strengthened advocacy efforts for labor protections, the formalization of the informal economy, and the promotion of gender-responsive policies. These initiatives are designed to lift workers out of poverty, ensuring better wages, improved social protections, and safe working environments.

By focusing on strengthening social dialogue and increasing the representational capacity of workers&apos; organizations, this intervention seeks to build more resilient local economies. The beneficiaries of this strategy are the workers, particularly those in vulnerable situations, who will gain benefits from organized labor representation and the protection of their rights. The long-term vision encompasses fostering a more equitable and inclusive economy, ultimately contributing to sustainable development in Burundi. Through coordinated efforts and strategic partnerships, the ILO aims to create transformative change that addresses systemic challenges and enhances social justice for Burundian workers.</narrative>
  </description>
